# Secrets must never enter an image layer: layers persist in /var/lib/docker
# after the source file is rotated or deleted, and `docker history`/`docker save`
# recovers them from any dangling image - so a baked secret outlives its own
# rotation. The runtime gets these values from compose's `env_file:` instead
# (see docker-compose.yml). `.git` is deliberately NOT excluded: it carries no
# secrets (.env has never been tracked) and core/version.py shells out to it for
# the admin update-check and the development self-update action.
.env*
!.env-sample

__pycache__
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.cache
*_cache/
*.log
*~
*.out
db.sqlite
dist/
build/
pgsql/
node_modules/
docs/
downloads/
venv/
